{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550923-reckoning-of-new-york","id":1550923,"title":"Reckoning of New York","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-10T16:49:44-07:00","id":1550923,"title":"Reckoning of New York","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> Anyone pick up the third visual novel for V:TM on Steam? It's also on consoles. I enjoyed COTERIES OF NEW YORK but hated the ending. I felt SHADOWS OF NEW YORK was an improvement in almost every way. RECKONING OF NEW YORK is something of a mixed bag that I think is squarely in the middle.<br /> <br /> This time around it's sort of like Resident Evil 2 in that you play two separate characters going through the same events. The first time you play as Kali, who is a hyperactive sarcastic Ravnos, and then the same events as Padraic, a Caitiff, but with added context to everyhing.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of whether or not you like this game will depend on whether or not you enjoy Kali's type of character. She is a lot closer to the kind of player characters I have at my game who have a bunch of energy versus the dark and depressing but cool Julia from Shadows.<br /> <br /> However, it does bring back feeding and that's a good thing, IMHO.<br /> <br /> This definitely feels like the last of the Draw Distance visual novels and probably for the best. The limitations of the design show up in how everything is on the railroad throughout. Literally, the only decision that really matters is the last one in the second campaign.<br /> <br /> But it's probably the best Non-OPP product other than LA by Night.<br /> <br /> If they were to continue these, I hope they'd do Chicago/Gary as the setting for the visual novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Ph